From 02a66427c7096444d53fbbaf655d469f6cdcd7f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yago Lasse <yagolasse@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:12:01 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] linux: case-insensitive guest paths, [PATH] line on POSIX

Xbox file systems ignore case; a title opens d:\FRONT\MOVIES\MIDWAY.SFD while
an extracted disc may hold front/movies/midway.sfd. The POSIX backend now
resolves each component after the base dir that doesn't exist as spelled to
the first directory entry matching it ignoring case; the walk stops at the
first component with no match (a file about to be created keeps its spelling).

It also prints the [PATH] line and calls g_xbox_path_hook as the Win32
backend does, so tools keyed on that line work on both.

New fixture tests/kernel_path_case_posix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MpLs2w6Qd9WdNHUWmKSXXn
